{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>A generation crooked and perverse.</b> He is speaking now about Israel, and this is joined with 'Is it to YHWH that you requite this,' even though Scripture separates them by the end of a verse — he says: even though you are a crooked and perverse generation and desire to corrupt yourselves like them, is it to YHWH that you requite this? And since he had already mentioned above (Deuteronomy 31:27), 'for after my death you will deal corruptly,' and informed them in his prophecy that they are destined to deal corruptly and worship idolatry after the death of Joshua, he therefore adds to them and warns them about this."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:53:01.618907205Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}